 L106.0 -24.6 L107.3 -17.9 L93.5 -12.9Z M18.4 0a18.4 18.4 0 1 0 -36.9 0a18.4 18.4 0 1 0 36.9 0Z M60.3 39.8a20.5 20.5 0 1 0 -41.0 0a20.5 20.5 0 1 0 41.0 0Z M-19.3 39.8a20.5 20.5 0 1 0 -41.0 0a20.5 20.5 0 1 0 41.0 0Z M-19.3 -39.8a20.5 20.5 0 1 0 -41.0 0a20.5 20.5 0 1 0 41.0 0Z M60.3 -39.8a20.5 20.5 0 1 0 -41.0 0a20.5 20.5 0 1 0 41.0 0Z" class="gC" fill-rule="evenodd"/></g></g><circle cx="220.0" cy="380.0" r="9" class="gJ"/><circle cx="357.3" cy="264.8" r="6" class="gJ"/><circle cx="493.3" cy="228.4" r="8" class="gJ"/></svg><p class="gb-hero-cap">Scroll to wind the train &middot; 44 &rarr; 12 &rarr; 32 teeth</p></div></div><div class="gb-hero-s" aria-hidden="true"><span>Scroll</span><i></i></div></section>

<div class="gb-mq mq" aria-hidden="true"><div><span>Mainspring</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Barrel</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Centre wheel</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Third wheel</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Fourth wheel</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Escape wheel</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Pallet fork</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Balance</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Hairspring</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Jewels</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Rotor</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Keyless works</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Mainspring</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Barrel</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Centre wheel</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Third wheel</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Fourth wheel</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Escape wheel</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Pallet fork</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Balance</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Hairspring</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Jewels</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Rotor</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i><span>Keyless works</span><i aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</i></div></div>

<section class="gb-pp" id="path"><div class="gb-pp-st"><div class="gb-w gb-pp-h"><p class="gb-ey"><span></span>The power path</p><h2>From your thumb on the crown to the tip of the seconds hand</h2><div class="gb-pp-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i id="pp-b"></i></div></div><div class="gb-pp-tr" id="pp-t"><div class="gb-pc"><span class="gb-pc-n">01</span><div class="gb-pc-v"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1612263731558-bbac49f8581a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=420&q=75" alt="a close view of the steel plates and gears of a watch movement" width="560" height="420" loading="lazy"></div><h3>Mainspring</h3><p>A coiled ribbon of alloy inside the barrel stores the energy you give the watch when you wind it. As it slowly unwinds it turns the barrel, which drives everything else.</p></div><div class="gb-pc"><span class="gb-pc-n">02</span><div class="gb-pc-v"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1593153041370-5ebf6b82886a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=420&q=75" alt="hundreds of small brass watch gears scattered together" width="560" height="420" loading="lazy"></div><h3>Gear train</h3><p>A chain of wheels and pinions steps the slow turn of the barrel up into faster turns, so one wheel rotates once an hour and another once a minute.</p></div><div class="gb-pc"><span class="gb-pc-n">03</span><div class="gb-pc-v"><svg viewBox="0 0 200 150" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M60 20l40 55 40-55M100 75v60" class="sv"/><circle cx="100" cy="75" r="8" class="sf"/></svg></div><h3>Escapement</h3><p>The escape wheel and pallet fork let the gear train advance one tooth at a time, and give the balance a small push on every swing so it never stops.</p></div><div class="gb-pc"><span class="gb-pc-n">04</span><div class="gb-pc-v"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1629135458283-0c69f7cead37?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=420&q=75" alt="gold watch wheels and red jewel bearings" width="560" height="420" loading="lazy"></div><h3>Balance &amp; hairspring</h3><p>A weighted wheel on a fine spring swings back and forth at a steady rate. Each swing is a beat, and the beats are what the watch actually counts.</p></div><div class="gb-pc"><span class="gb-pc-n">05</span><div class="gb-pc-v"><svg viewBox="0 0 200 150" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="100" cy="75" r="62" class="sv"/><path d="M100 75V24M100 75l34 20" class="sv sk"/><circle cx="100" cy="75" r="6" class="sf"/></svg></div><h3>Motion works &amp; hands</h3><p>Under the dial, a small set of wheels divides the minute wheel's turn by twelve so the hour hand moves at its own slower pace.</p></div></div></div></section>

<section class="gb-s gb-bt" id="beat"><div class="gb-w gb-bt-g"><div class="gb-bt-v"><svg viewBox="0 0 320 320" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="160" cy="160" r="150" class="dl"/><g id="bt-ticks"></g><text x="160" y="112" class="dn">GEARBOX</text><text x="160" y="226" class="dv" id="bt-dv">28,800 vph</text><line x1="160" y1="182" x2="160" y2="30" class="sh" id="bt-h"/><circle cx="160" cy="160" r="7" class="hc"/></svg><div class="gb-bal"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" aria-hidden="true"><g id="bt-bw"><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="48" class="bw"/><path d="M60 12v96M12 60h96" class="bw"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="6" class="hc"/></g><path id="bt-hs" d="M60 60m-4 0a4 4 0 1 1 8 0a8 8 0 1 1-16 0a12 12 0 1 1 24 0a16 16 0 1 1-32 0" class="hs"/></svg><span>Balance, slowed 10&times;</span></div></div>
<div><p class="gb-ey"><span></span>Tool 01 &middot; Beat rate visualiser</p><h2 class="rv">Why a mechanical seconds hand <em>sweeps</em></h2><p class="gb-p">A mechanical seconds hand is not gliding. It jumps forward on every beat of the balance, several times a second. Pick a beat rate and watch the hand, then compare it with a quartz watch that steps once a second.</p>
<div class="gb-chips" role="group" aria-label="Beat rate"><button type="button" data-v="18000">18,000</button><button type="button" data-v="21600">21,600</button><button type="button" data-v="25200">25,200</button><button type="button" data-v="28800" class="on">28,800</button><button type="button" data-v="36000">36,000</button><button type="button" data-v="3600">Quartz</button></div>
<dl class="gb-read" aria-live="polite"><div><dt>Frequency</dt><dd id="bt-hz">4 Hz</dd></div><div><dt>Steps per second</dt><dd id="bt-bs">8</dd></div><div><dt>Beats per day</dt><dd id="bt-bd">691,200</dd></div><div><dt>Each step</dt><dd id="bt-st">0.125 s</dd></div></dl><p class="gb-note" id="bt-n"></p></div></div></section>

<section class="gb-s gb-rt" id="ratio"><div class="gb-w"><div class="gb-rt-h"><div><p class="gb-ey"><span></span>Tool 02 &middot; Gear ratio calculator</p><h2 class="rv">Count the teeth, <em>find the speed</em></h2></div><p class="gb-p">When a wheel drives a smaller pinion, the pinion turns faster by the ratio of their teeth. Set the teeth and how fast the driving wheel turns, or load a real stage from a typical watch.</p></div>
<div class="gb-rt-g"><div class="gb-rt-f"><div class="gb-pre" role="group" aria-label="Typical stages"><button type="button" data-p="80,10,1">Centre &rarr; third</button><button type="button" data-p="75,10,8">Third &rarr; fourth</button><button type="button" data-p="80,8,60">Fourth &rarr; escape</button></div>
<label for="rt-a">Driving wheel teeth<input id="rt-a" type="number" min="6" max="150" value="80"></label><label for="rt-b">Driven pinion teeth<input id="rt-b" type="number" min="6" max="150" value="10"></label><label for="rt-s">Driving wheel turns per hour<input id="rt-s" type="number" min="0.1" max="600" step="0.1" value="1"></label>
<div class="gb-rt-o" aria-live="polite"><b id="rt-r">8 : 1</b><p id="rt-t"></p></div></div><div class="gb-rt-v"><svg viewBox="0 0 560 340" id="rt-svg" aria-hidden="true"><g id="rt-ga"><path id="rt-pa" class="gA2" fill-rule="evenodd"/></g><g id="rt-gb"><path id="rt-pb" class="gB2" fill-rule="evenodd"/></g></svg><p class="gb-hero-cap">Animated at 600&times; real speed</p></div></div></div></section>

